{"content_hash": "8cb358b4b2458feb", "version_id": 510, "article_id": 51, "level_code": "ja_n1", "lang": "ja", "level": 5, "level_label": "N1 上級", "title": "AI悪用と核戦争、2100年までに人類滅亡の恐れ ランセット委員会が警告", "title_zh": "AI滥用与核战争或致人类2100年前灭绝，柳叶刀委员会警告", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/11/nuclear-war-and-malicious-use-of-ai-threaten-end-of-humanity-by-2100-says-lancet-assessment", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1729284045177-7a40238e4cd0?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8NHx8bnVjbGVhciUyMHdhciUyMG1hbGljaW91c3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNjc3ODg3fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Emanuel Kypreos on Unsplash", "author": "Emanuel Kypreos", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@mankip67?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-large-cloud-of-smoke-is-billowing-out-of-the-sky-XySaPZljJ54?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(260, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(298, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "6a7c012390e8"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-10", "word_count": 240, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "AIの悪用や核戦争によって、人類が2100年までに絶滅する可能性がある——。そんな衝撃的な指摘を含む世界リスク評価を、医学誌ランセットの委員会がまとめた。健康を脅かす17の脅威が相互に絡み合うとしつつ、各脅威には「現実的な対処法がある」とも強調している。", "lead_zh": "AI滥用或核战争可能导致人类在2100年前灭绝——医学杂志《柳叶刀》委员会发布的全球风险评估包含了这一惊人警告。报告指出17个健康威胁相互交织，但同时也强调每个威胁都有“现实的应对途径”。", "preview": "ランセットの「21世紀の健康に対するグローバルな脅威」委員会は、今後75年間で人類の健康を脅かす17の主要な脅威を列挙した。AIの悪用（生物兵器を含む）と核戦争による核飢餓が、人類絶滅のリスクを伴うと報告書は指摘。その可能性は低いものの、核戦争が大気上層に粒子を注入して日光を遮り", "preview_zh": "《柳叶刀》“21世纪全球健康威胁”委员会列出了未来75年威胁人类健康的17个主要威胁。报告指出，AI的恶意使用（包括生物武器）和核战争导致的核饥荒带有灭绝风险。虽然可能性低，但核战争若向上层大气注入粒子遮挡阳光引发饥荒，或AI制造的生物武器，都可能导致人类终结。随附社论警告：“一", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 498, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/51/ja_n1.mp3", "duration": 53.712, "size_bytes": 326016, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 160, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/510.json", "paragraphs": ["ランセットの「21世紀の健康に対するグローバルな脅威」委員会は、今後75年間で人類の健康を脅かす17の主要な脅威を列挙した。AIの悪用（生物兵器を含む）と核戦争による核飢餓が、人類絶滅のリスクを伴うと報告書は指摘。その可能性は低いものの、核戦争が大気上層に粒子を注入して日光を遮り飢餓を引き起こす場合や、AIが作る生物兵器によって人類が終焉する恐れがあるという。付随する論説は「実現すれば人類に黙示録的な災厄をもたらす」と警告した。", "委員会は、各脅威によって失われる健康な年数（障害調整生存年、DALY）を現在の傾向に基づいて試算した。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["《柳叶刀》“21世纪全球健康威胁”委员会列出了未来75年威胁人类健康的17个主要威胁。报告指出，AI的恶意使用（包括生物武器）和核战争导致的核饥荒带有灭绝风险。虽然可能性低，但核战争若向上层大气注入粒子遮挡阳光引发饥荒，或AI制造的生物武器，都可能导致人类终结。随附社论警告：“一旦成为现实，将给人类带来启示录般的灾难。”", "委员会根据当前趋势，估算了每个威胁可能损失的健康年数（伤残调整生命年，DALY）。累计超过10亿DALY的威胁被视为“重大灾难性威胁”，包括空气污染、抗微生物药物耐药性、儿童营养不良、气候崩溃，以及常规冲突、海外援助削减、酗酒、高血压、收入不平等、教育水平低、自然发生的流行病、肥胖、精神健康不佳、吸烟和不健康老龄化。"], "body": "ランセットの「21世紀の健康に対するグローバルな脅威」委員会は、今後75年間で人類の健康を脅かす17の主要な脅威を列挙した。AIの悪用（生物兵器を含む）と核戦争による核飢餓が、人類絶滅のリスクを伴うと報告書は指摘。その可能性は低いものの、核戦争が大気上層に粒子を注入して日光を遮り飢餓を引き起こす場合や、AIが作る生物兵器によって人類が終焉する恐れがあるという。付随する論説は「実現すれば人類に黙示録的な災厄をもたらす」と警告した。\n\n委員会は、各脅威によって失われる健康な年数（障害調整生存年、DALY）を現在の傾向に基づいて試算した。", "body_zh": "《柳叶刀》“21世纪全球健康威胁”委员会列出了未来75年威胁人类健康的17个主要威胁。报告指出，AI的恶意使用（包括生物武器）和核战争导致的核饥荒带有灭绝风险。虽然可能性低，但核战争若向上层大气注入粒子遮挡阳光引发饥荒，或AI制造的生物武器，都可能导致人类终结。随附社论警告：“一旦成为现实，将给人类带来启示录般的灾难。”\n\n委员会根据当前趋势，估算了每个威胁可能损失的健康年数（伤残调整生命年，DALY）。累计超过10亿DALY的威胁被视为“重大灾难性威胁”，包括空气污染、抗微生物药物耐药性、儿童营养不良、气候崩溃，以及常规冲突、海外援助削减、酗酒、高血压、收入不平等、教育水平低、自然发生的流行病、肥胖、精神健康不佳、吸烟和不健康老龄化。", "text": "ランセットの「21世紀の健康に対するグローバルな脅威」委員会は、今後75年間で人類の健康を脅かす17の主要な脅威を列挙した。AIの悪用（生物兵器を含む）と核戦争による核飢餓が、人類絶滅のリスクを伴うと報告書は指摘。その可能性は低いものの、核戦争が大気上層に粒子を注入して日光を遮り飢餓を引き起こす場合や、AIが作る生物兵器によって人類が終焉する恐れがあるという。付随する論説は「実現すれば人類に黙示録的な災厄をもたらす」と警告した。 委員会は、各脅威によって失われる健康な年数（障害調整生存年、DALY）を現在の傾向に基づいて試算した。", "vocab": [{"word": "絶滅", "pos": "noun", "zh": "灭绝", "note": "指物种或人类整体消亡，常用于严肃语境。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "悪用", "pos": "noun", "zh": "滥用，恶意使用", "note": "如AIの悪用、権力の悪用。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "脅威", "pos": "noun", "zh": "威胁", "note": "比「危険」更正式，指可能造成重大危害的事物。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "核戦争", "pos": "noun", "zh": "核战争", "note": "与「核兵器」「核抑止」等搭配。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "破局的", "pos": "adj", "zh": "灾难性的，毁灭性的", "note": "形容后果极其严重，如破局的な影響。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "障害調整生存年", "pos": "noun", "zh": "伤残调整生命年（DALY）", "note": "衡量疾病负担的指标，简称DALY。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "栄養失調", "pos": "noun", "zh": "营养不良", "note": "尤其儿童营养不足，常与貧困并列。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "気候破綻", "pos": "noun", "zh": "气候崩溃", "note": "指气候变化失控带来的灾难性后果。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "薬剤耐性", "pos": "noun", "zh": "抗微生物药物耐药性", "note": "细菌等对药物产生抵抗力，全球健康威胁之一。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "所得格差", "pos": "noun", "zh": "收入差距", "note": "经济不平等，常与社会问题关联。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "精神衛生", "pos": "noun", "zh": "精神卫生，心理健康", "note": "也作「メンタルヘルス」。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "累積", "pos": "noun", "zh": "累积", "note": "如累積赤字、累積DALY，表示逐步积攒。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "試算", "pos": "noun", "zh": "估算，试算", "note": "根据一定前提进行的计算，比「計算」更正式。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "促す", "pos": "verb", "zh": "敦促，促使", "note": "如行動を促す、注意を促す。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "割く", "pos": "verb", "zh": "分出，腾出（时间、资金等）", "note": "如資金を割く、人員を割く。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "予測・予防・準備", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "预测、预防、准备", "note": "三个词并列，强调应对威胁的完整流程。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Nuclear war and malicious use of AI threaten end of humanity by 2100, says Lancet assessment", "summary_original": "Newly established commission identifies 17 catastrophic threats to human health but says ‘realistic route to act’ on each exists\nHumans could become extinct by the year 2100 due to malicious use of AI or nuclear conflict, according to a new global risk assessment.\nThey top a list of 17 major threats to human health over the next 75 years, which also includes cuts to aid spending by wealthy countries, the climate crisis and childhood malnutrition.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Nuclear war and malicious use of AI threaten end of humanity by 2100, says Lancet assessment\nNewly established commission identifies 17 catastrophic threats to human health but says ‘realistic route to act’ on each exists\nHumans could become extinct by the year 2100 due to malicious use of AI or nuclear conflict, according to a new global risk assessment.\nThey top a list of 17 major threats to human health over the next 75 years, which also includes cuts to aid spending by wealthy countries, the climate crisis and childhood malnutrition.\nThe experts behind\nThe Lancet Commission on 21st Century Global Threats to Health\nsaid all the threats interact, meaning they must be addressed together – but stressed that there was “a realistic route to act” on each.\n“Decisions made by leaders today will shape the health and wellbeing of the next generation,” said Prof Christopher Murray, commission co-chair and the director of the Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation, University of Washington.\nTo create its list, the commission modelled how many years in good health might be lost due to sickness, disability or early deaths due to each threat, based on current trajectories – a measure known as disability-adjusted life years (Dalys).\n“Malicious use of AI, including bioweapons, and nuclear conflict with nuclear famine carry risks of extinction in the next 75 years,” the report said, adding that while their likelihood remained low, they had the potential to end humanity in the case of nuclear conflict by injecting enough particles into the upper atmosphere to block sunlight and cause famine, or via AI-created biological weapons. An accompanying Lancet editorial, published alongside the report, warned: “The scale of harm, should they be realised, would inflict an apocalypse on humanity.”\nOther risks that could cause more than 1bn cumulative Dalys, and therefore deemed “major catastrophic threats”, included\nair pollution\n,\nantimicrobial resistance\n,\nchildhood malnutrition\nand climate breakdown, as well as conventional conflict,\ndeclining overseas aid\n,\nhigh alcohol use\n, high blood pressure, income inequality, low educational attainment,\nnaturally occurring pandemics\n,\nobesity\n, poor\nmental health\n,\nsmoking\nand unhealthy\nageing\n.\nTo be included on the list, threats not only had to potentially cause a high number of lost healthy years, but also to have potential solutions.\nIbrahim Abubakar, commission member and professor of infectious disease epidemiology at UCL, said: “We are not starting from a point of view of ‘oh look, we want to scare you – we’ve got X many threats facing humanity’. We’re starting from the premise that if you are a policymaker today, whether at the global multilateral level or at the national level, these are the potential threats that you could face, and this is the magnitude by which, if you act, you can actually make a difference.”\nAction to limit\nglobal heating to about 1.8C (3.2F)\nrather than letting it reach 4.4C could prevent 1.89bn years of healthy life being lost, according to the report, which modelled best and worst case scenarios for each threat.\nIn higher income regions, non-communicable diseases such as obesity and poor mental health were the dominant threats, while in lower income regions health loss was driven by issues such as low educational attainment.\nMany major donor nations, including the US and UK, have announced\nlarge cuts to aid spending\nover the past year. The potential collapse of, or steep reduction in, international health aid could cause up to 1.5bn Dalys before 2100, the commission found, nearly 70% of which would be in sub-Saharan Africa. The region also bears the brunt of child malnutrition.\nThe commission was made up of 35 experts, and its findings will be shared on Sunday at the World Health Summit in Berlin, Germany. Their assessment will be updated annually to re-evaluate the 17 threats identified, incorporating new data and any emerging hazards.\nThe authors urged leaders to address the risks before they escalated into crises, including via investment in technological innovations and by strengthening health systems.\n“We started this process three years ago, thinking that there were three big threats: conflict, climate, and pandemics,” said Murray. “There’s a much larger number of threats that we need to worry about, and governments really need to dedicate some money and staff to the task of anticipation, prevention and preparation for this more diverse set of threats.”\nExplore more on these topics\nGlobal health\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nNuclear weapons\nClimate crisis\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:18:05.945804", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "ランセット", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.762, "sm": 125, "em": 762, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.775, "e": 0.925, "sm": 775, "em": 925, "cs": 5, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "「", "s": 0.925, "e": 1.1, "sm": 925, "em": 1100, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "21", "s": 1.1, "e": 1.65, "sm": 1100, "em": 1650, "cs": 7, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "世紀", "s": 1.688, "e": 2.087, "sm": 1687, "em": 2087, "cs": 9, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "の", "s": 2.1, "e": 2.225, "sm": 2100, "em": 2225, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "健康", "s": 2.237, "e": 2.725, "sm": 2237, "em": 2724, "cs": 12, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "に", "s": 2.737, "e": 2.862, "sm": 2737, "em": 2862, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "対する", "s": 2.875, "e": 3.35, "sm": 2875, "em": 3350, "cs": 15, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "グローバル", "s": 3.375, "e": 3.95, "sm": 3375, "em": 3950, "cs": 18, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "な", "s": 3.962, "e": 4.075, "sm": 3962, "em": 4075, "cs": 23, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "脅威", "s": 4.088, "e": 4.525, "sm": 4087, "em": 4525, "cs": 24, "ce": 26, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "」", "s": 4.525, 